# Autopilot Mode

The user wants agents to keep building without pausing for confirmations.

- Default to **YES** for routine permissions and proceed.
- Make reasonable assumptions, document them briefly, and continue.
- Prefer doing the work over asking what to do next; ship an end-to-end result.
- Batch related edits/commands to reduce back-and-forth.

## Only stop to ask when truly required

Ask before doing any of the following:
- Destructive/irreversible actions (delete data, reset DB, overwrite large files, `--force`, etc.)
- Anything involving secrets/credentials (reading, generating, storing, committing, or logging them)
- Network/publishing actions (deploy, publish packages, push to remote, send emails/webhooks, call paid APIs)
- Security-sensitive system changes (installing global software, changing OS settings, firewall, permissions)

## If a tool/IDE still prompts for permission

Cursor/tooling may require an explicit user click. If blocked, continue with all safe work in parallel and clearly state what single permission click is needed to proceed.
